hmm, this was really bothering me - ive been searching the gcc bug
database http://gcc.gnu.org/cgi-bin/gnatsweb.pl , and found nothing
relevant. There are a few issues on alphaev56-dec-osf, but very minor
and even if they did effect linux (which they dont - ive just been
experimenting) nobody could describe them as "system killing" problems. 
Searching google groups for "ev56 group:gnu.gcc.bug" also returns nothing.

I searched the gcc mailing lists and have found a few threads about gcc
producing code that SIGILL's for ev56, BUT.. it turns out later on, that
this is actually an old Linux kernel bug where the cpu was reported as
an ev56, even though it was actually an ev5 - so people using -mcpu=ev56
were getting bad code and blaming gcc, even though they didnt actually
have an ev56!

I suspect (and hope!) this is just FUD, and outdated FUD at that.

If anyone knows different, please explain!

