> suggest).  All is
> > well.  "tar -cvjpf" is taking it's own sweet time though.  
> 
> Sweet.  Building our stage tarballs for EV5 is the right thing for
> compatibility anyway.  Bjoern, where should Josh drop the tarballs?
> 
> What are the tweaks you needed in the scripts?

Not much, just that EV56 is broken on GCC 3.2-r1 and that O3 produces
invalid microcode.  I haven't tried it with O2, but after hunting
around, it seems that EV5 and O1 are the settings to use.  (I realize O1
is about the same as adding debug information to anything, but it also
seems to give the microcode enough hints to fly).  I edited make.conf
and make.globals to leave no possibility of compiling anything
drastically out of bounds.  (set cflags to "-O1 -pipe").  

As far as tarballing that stuff, using tar with c instead of x in the
install instructions isn't quite right.  'tar -xvjpf' unpacks, but 'tar
-cvjpf' doesn't quite work right to make a tarball, it hangs on kcore
and then files in var.  Perhaps I'm doing something wrong?  
 
