Seemant Kulleen wrote:[Sun Feb 23 2003, 11:14:50PM EST]
> I have an alpha here, it's running Gentoo 1.4rc_2 (after you're done
> with rc_1's stage 1, you end up with an rc_2 stage 2 tarball, correct?)
> for the EV56 with -O1.  Being an alpha, GCC produces middling quality
> code with better then O1, to my understanding.
>=20
> My question is twofold:  Is Gentoo interested in continued Alpha work?

Yes, definitely.  The only problem right now is that we're short-staffed
on Alpha developers.  The three are basically bjb, wwoods, and myself.
However all three of us are pretty involved at our jobs, too, so when
we're all busy, gentoo/alpha stalls for a while.

For the most part, we split up like this:

    bjb      - kernel, linker, gcc
    wwoods   - kde, misc apps
    agriffis - gnome, misc apps

However we all dabble around since there's no shortage of bugs.

> If so, I'll contribute in my spare time. =20

Please please do.

> I have two alpha systems here
> and a pretty good idea of how they work.  ;-)

I'm just curious, why the ;-) ?  Do you have a background working on
alpha?

> Second question is, if
> so, where shall I put this stage2 I made?  And following that, stage 3?
> (Sometime next year, compiling is slow as balls on the alpha...)

That's a good question.  I think bjb would be the best to answer but
he's been MIA for a few weeks at the moment.  (He tells me he's planning
to get back to Gentoo soon.)

Part of the problem for me is that I'm not very familiar with the
stages, livecd's, etc.  Here we use a bootp image that Chouser hacked up
once (and it just keeps working).  We're planning to make the bootp
image publicly available when we can find the time...

Aron



